taking the class and walking it walking  into the class in the first day with  Seth and Sarah was an introduction to a  more radical notion but the way I was  excited about a self-generated world and  dreams had really tight parallels in  waking life that this is a  self-generated world and in much the  same way that there are fundamental  rules to my vision and to my audition  that created my world that I am a world  creator as much as a world experiencer  and it's it's not a new notion for me in  a sense but what was really new is the  idea that you could have experiences  like something as simple as a ganzfeld  ping-pong ball experience and then you  could start to see those rules  um they talked a lot about perceiving  perception but how is it that we can  reveal the fundamental building blocks  of our experience to ourselves through  these sorts of experiential experiments  and so the notion that waking life is a  generated dream the notion that you can  sit between logic and illogic subjective  and objective in your day-to-day  experience for me was a really tight tie  and I don't want to take too much time  because I think the talk is gonna be a  lot of fun but that sort of meeting  ground sleeping as the way of seeing  sleeping as a way of seeing yourself  generating your world yourself  generating your visual world your  semantic world using experimentation as  a form of self investigation of those  initial fundamental rules those  fundamentally constructive experiences  and then coming to class and seeing  you're doing it when you're awake too  and you you have to mix art and science  you have to mix experience an experiment  to really get at this intersection was  super exciting for me so so yeah um I  hope you have a lot of fun talking about  seeing internal and external  when I wish all the best and I'm sorry I  can't beat it all right
 

